Package: bayestrials
Title: Bayesian Adaptive Clinical Trials: Design, Calibration and Simulation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nicholas G.", "Polson", role = "aut"),
    person("Vadim", "Sokolov", email = "vsokolov@gmu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Companion package to the book "Bayesian Adaptive Clinical Trials". Posterior computations for binary, normal and time-to-event endpoints; group sequential boundaries by the Armitage recursion; calibration of posterior probability success rules to a frequentist type I error by simulation; operating characteristics of fixed, group sequential and Bayesian adaptive designs; predictive probability and backward induction; response-adaptive randomization; dose finding; borrowing from historical data; platform trials; e-values; and the case-study reconstructions used in the book.
URL: https://github.com/VadimSokolov/bayestrials
BugReports: https://github.com/VadimSokolov/bayestrials/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: stats, parallel
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), patchwork, rpact, gsDesign, BOIN
Config/testthat/edition: 3
LazyData: true
